\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Arena runs of build v0.1.0: rows \texttt  {fuzz-random-v0.1}, \texttt  {fuzz-greedy-v0.1} and \texttt  {v0.1-vs-minimax-real-clock} of RESULTS.md, in that order; opponents are the starter's \texttt  {baselines/random}, \texttt  {greedy} and \texttt  {minimax}. Openings: \texttt  {data/openings.txt}. The tool printed no Elo for these runs. Loads of 7--10 during the fuzz runs are expected with twelve workers and mean those games do not measure time management; the minimax run used four workers (load 1.5--3.9 on 16 cores), so its per-move times are indicative but it is not the solo pass of Stage 3. Its one draw is by threefold repetition; the PGNs are kept under \texttt  {data/pgn/}. \texttt  {baselines/greedy} searches one ply on material; \texttt  {baselines/minimax} two plies on material and mobility with no time management {\small  (source: README.md)}.}}{13}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
